that was so cool that was so awesome how  exactly does one prepare for an  interdimensional fight with a  telekinetic demon all the cast members  of stranger things had to do their own  individual prep for certain scenes and  moments let's find out who had to  undergo intense physical training mental  preparation and learning a brand new  skill we actually went on a 45 minute  walk that day do you remember number one  we think jamie campbell bower may be a  bit of a psychopath bower didn't know  anything about his character before his  audition so he decided to create his own  origin story for henry which impressed  the duffer brothers he drew inspiration  for his performance from horror classics  such as hellraiser and primal fear but  the craziest thing bauer did to prepare  was to make a board with all the faces  of the stranger things cast i went a bit  nuts for like two days he put will byers  in the center and surrounded him with  co-stars pics of the upside down and  horror icons like dracula needless to  say bower was thrilled when he got the  role there was like a sigh of relief it  was like tears  it was a big deal number two eddie was  the master of the upside down which  required joseph quinn to master master  of puppets i didn't think i'd ever be  able to kind of fulfill this kind of  quite adolescent fantasy of being a rock  star luckily quinn had a solid  foundation in guitar playing having  taken lessons when he was younger it  helped him shred out the metallica song  as he stated that most of the playing  was actually him they only had another  guitarist come in to perform the more  difficult solo besides that quinn was a  true rock star i had a bash at it number  three how many times can you listen to  your favorite song without getting sick  of it that's the question sadie sings  set out to find to prepare for her  season 4 return as max the walkman we  see in the show is real and had a real  cassette playing running up that hill  sync figured that she had to really  experience what her character was going  through she listened to the song  constantly around set and even spent an  entire day listening to it on repeat did  she get sick of it i cannot even tell  you how many times i've listened to  running up that hill it's been a lot but  i'm still not sick of it which is good  number four being held in a secret  russian prison is a great way to lose  weight david harbour can attest he lost  80 pounds from season 3 when he was 270  but weighed in for the fourth season at  190. his intense prep to lose the weight  included pilates and a whole lot of  fasting it took 8 months for him to drop  the weight but the most impressive part  he lost the weight before the show was  shut down due to kovid meaning he had to  maintain his new weight for an entire  year i don't think i'll ever do that  again  number five everybody knows the best way  to clear your head is to take a nice  long walk that's exactly what matthew  modine and millie bobby brown did the  day they had to film brenner's demise it  was a very sad day for us both the love  these two have for each other is genuine  so they decided to take a 45 minute walk  together to get into the right headspace  for the scene i honestly love millie  bobby brown number six  sometimes the mental prep is more  difficult than the physical caleb  mclaughlin had to prepare his mind for  max's goodbye because as we saw it was  very intense and emotional  i prepared for it mentally it was a long  day mclaughlin said he started preparing  for the scene two weeks prior to filming  on top of this he had to do the attic  fight scene with jason right beforehand  that is a lot to handle i think i  definitely prepared for this because  it was a sequence that i had to like  rehearse number seven when the cameras  are pointed squarely on you and all the  eyes in the room are fixated on your  person getting nervous seems like a  guarantee finn wolfhard found this out  when he had to deliver his monologue to  millie during the finale i  was like super scared about it so i like  ran it in my head over and over again  and i was i wanted to be like  as off book as i could it was a ton of  prep but it paid off they got the scene  done in a couple of takes and wolfhard  even had room to improvise the you're my  superhero yeah it was fun it was really  fun to do number eight what isn't steve  good at all the way back in the ancient  times of season 1 the brothers duff told  joe kiri that he was going to have to  film a swimming scene as part of the  school team which involved wearing a  speedo so joe wasted no time preparing  he got into great shape and took  swimming lessons to be at the peak of  his physical form it's like oh my god i  have to like get in shape and did all  these swimming lessons and you know like  i was paying for all this stuff and then  the duffer brothers decided to cut the  scenes before they even shot them  however his prep eventually paid off as  he put his skills to use during the late  scene in season 4. number 9 we honestly  don't know why this next one is  necessary the scene when charlie  heaton's jonathan and eduardo franco's  argyle or hitting golf balls into a pile  of junk required more prep than you  would think they were sent to a country  club to practice their golfing skills  and franco wasn't too happy about what  they had to wear so costume like gave us  these like very yuppy golfing golfing  outfits to go  turn up to this country club in he  instated it was very difficult to get a  handle of it although we don't think the  audience was expecting perfect technique  from two stoners hitting golf balls at  junk cars it's actually super difficult  just hitting it was so hard like there's  so much technique number 10 eddie  munsten is the quintessential metalhead  but joseph quinn not so much before the  show he didn't have any interest in  metal or d d or nerd culture but that  doesn't mean he won't convert i'm open  to anything wow quinn drew inspiration  from spinal tap to get into the  headspace of a true metalhead i think  kind of just in terms of like how uh  being a metal head isn't a part-time gig  it's you've got to take it pretty  seriously number 11 becoming henry is  one thing transforming into an  interdimensional demon is a whole other  story let's just say jaime campbell  bower got well acquainted with the  makeup chair he spent seven to eight  hours every single time they needed to  apply the vechna prosthetics which  included roughly 2425  individual pieces prep started at 3am  and once it did it was a marathon vfx  artist barry gower stated he did go into  a zen-like mode during the application  process music was a big part of this  process for bower specifically heavy  death metal just because for me it was  something that i was using as a process  to kind of um  bring up what i needed to bring up and  on the complete other end of the  spectrum he would sometimes just read a  book a perfectly balanced process this  whole thing should be number 12 riding a  skateboard is not easy i still can't  ride one sadie sink had no choice but to  learn though as her character was  required to shred some crete sync had  never even been on a board before being  cast as max so she was unsurprisingly  scared to hop on yeah it was pretty  daunting once i actually got on the  board i was like oh my god this is going  to be a lot harder than i thought it  would be but she wasn't alone finn  wolfhard a seasoned skater himself would  sometimes join her during her training  sessions which is just so freaking sweet  and these were no easy sessions it was  hard i had to like work at it for  three four months or something like that  it was every day for three hours during  that span and whenever she had a second  of free time she was ripping it  we commend the dedication the stranger  things cast has put into their roles  their preparation definitely paid off as  they delivered outstanding performances  that leave us wanting more which  preparation method did you find most  impressive let us know in the comments  and thanks for stopping by at the things
 

